Cloud computing has some general knowledge benefits such as High Availability and scalability. Lets get into detail on the benefits of cloud computing.

High Availability.
When deploying resources in the cloud, it is important that those resources are available when needed. 
High availability defines how available those resources are regardless of disruptions, natural disasters or hardware failures. 
It is often included in the service level agreement as the agreed upon policy to define how long the downtime will be per year.

Scalability.
Scalability is the ability to increase or decrease resources to meet demand. If you have a physical datacenter at traffic spikes, 
you cannot rapidly add more compute, storage or network resources because they have to be purchased. With cloud computing it is easier
to scale up or down and is often less costly because you pay for whta you consume. 

Vertical scaling
With vertical scaling, if you were developing an app and you needed more processing power, you could vertically 
scale up to add more CPUs or RAM to the virtual machine. Conversely, if you realized you had over-specified the needs, 
you could vertically scale down by lowering the CPU or RAM specifications.

Horizontal scaling
With horizontal scaling, if you suddenly experienced a steep jump in demand, your deployed resources could be scaled out 
(either automatically or manually). For example, you could add additional virtual machines or containers, scaling out. 
In the same manner, if there was a significant drop in demand, deployed resources could be scaled in (either automatically or manually), 
scaling in.

Reliability and predictability are also two important benefits that help you deploy resources with confidence.

Reliabiality
Reliablity is the ability of a system to recover from failures and be available to users readily. 
With availability zones, regions and region pairs that offer fault tolerance between physical hardware failuers and disasters, 
Your resources are highly available which makes cloud computing more reliable than on premises deployment.

Predictability
Predictability can be cost based or performance based. You can predict how much you will spend on resources that you utilize in the cloud instead 
of overestimating or underestimating hardware costs. Performance predictability means you can see exactly how much storage, compute or networking
resources you will need to have a good experience in your workflows.

Security and governance in the cloud.
Governance in the cloud help make sure your resources meet regulatory standards and are flagged if they do not. 
